Subject: Harden Fil-C compile-time rejections in Clang Sema, Driver, and FilPizlonator
Upstream-Base: llvmorg-23.1.6 (5b10d2d74929eae78912771222c9855af97496f4)
Fil-C-Head: cede3de02b42b58a14acc9ce39c9894ab952a915 (branch deluge)

In Release builds with LLVM_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS=OFF, llvm_unreachable() and
assert() compile away into UB or no-ops. Any user-input-reachable check that
relied on them could silently miscompile instead of rejecting the translation
unit (for example, __builtin_setjmp folded into FilPizlonator's default
intrinsic handler, making Ruby's autoconf probe succeed and panic at runtime).

Changes (from full audit of all 70 llvm_unreachable and 540 assert sites):
- clang/lib/Sema/SemaChecking.cpp: Reject __builtin_setjmp and __builtin_longjmp
  directly in Sema with err_builtin_setjmp_unsupported / err_builtin_longjmp_unsupported.
- llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/FilPizlonator.cpp: Replace all user-input-
  reachable llvm_unreachable and assert checks (eh.sjlj intrinsics, CallBrInst /
  asm goto, SEH funclet instructions, unlowered indirectbr, unsupported module
  inline asm, non-zero pointer address spaces, scalable vectors, 64-bit layout
  overflow checks in SafeAdd64/SafeMul64, defining reserved pass-through
  functions, incompatible setjmp prototypes, unsupported pointer atomicrmw,
  linkage, ConstantExpr, and catch-all unknown instructions) with
  report_fatal_error(..., /*GenCrashDiag=*/false).
- clang/lib/CodeGen/CGRecordLayoutBuilder.cpp: Replace non-zero address space
  assert and scalable vector unreachable with report_fatal_error.
- clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/Gnu.cpp: Replace GCC job refusal and linker
  version-script parse/EOF/write unreachables with report_fatal_error.

---
diff --git a/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGRecordLayoutBuilder.cpp b/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGRecordLayoutBuilder.cpp
index 242ac845b..f95b93f8c 100644
--- a/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGRecordLayoutBuilder.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGRecordLayoutBuilder.cpp
@@ -324,7 +324,10 @@ static bool hasPointers(llvm::Type* T) {
   }
 
   if (isa<llvm::PointerType>(T)) {
-    assert (!T->getPointerAddressSpace());
+    if (T->getPointerAddressSpace())
+      llvm::report_fatal_error(
+          "Fil-C does not support non-zero pointer address spaces",
+          /*GenCrashDiag=*/false);
     return true;
   }
 
@@ -344,8 +347,9 @@ static bool hasPointers(llvm::Type* T) {
     return hasPointers(VT->getElementType());
 
   if (isa<llvm::ScalableVectorType>(T)) {
-    llvm_unreachable("Shouldn't ever see scalable vectors in hasPtrs");
-    return false;
+    llvm::report_fatal_error(
+        "Fil-C does not support scalable vector types",
+        /*GenCrashDiag=*/false);
   }
     
   return false;
